name: Provider billing fraud
tagline: "A seeded payer program-integrity Link Analysis demo - referral kickbacks, phantom billing, a pill mill and upcoding, planted among 20 000 members, 1 500 providers and 80 000 claim lines with benign look-alikes"
description: "The health-insurer and public-payer program-integrity Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Nine synthetic feeds (address, owner, provider, provider_owner, member, claim_line, admission, referral, prescription; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 20 000 members, 1 500 providers and about 1 300 owners, about 81 000 claim lines, 2 800 hospital stays, 14 000 referrals and 30 000 prescriptions) are landed by nine Collectors and Pipelines. The health_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of six link kinds; the health_screen_links Job derives the four program-integrity screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-health-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by HealthLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-health-data.test.mjs): 2 practices send 85 % of their referrals to an imaging centre whose owner shares a home with one practice's owner; a physiotherapy clinic bills 40 patients for sessions while they were in hospital elsewhere or after they died; a pain clinic prescribes large strong-opioid quantities to 70 patients who live over 50 km away and mostly pay cash, filled at 2 pharmacies; 3 urgent-care clinics in 3 cities under one owner bill the top visit level about 4 times what their patients' ages predict. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a seaside practice referring to the only hospital nearby, a clinic whose date errors were reversed within a week, an oncology centre with local insured patients, and an elderly-care clinic whose patients really are over 80. Four saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: health.analyst lead, health.manager second approver, health.reviewer read-only, health.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the health_phantom_counts and health_phantom_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule health_billed_in_admission_or_after_death (on the shipped data it counts 159 open claim lines billed during an admission elsewhere or after death - 89 in a stay, 70 after a death - for 40 members, all at one physiotherapy clinic; never the 30 reversed date errors, the look-alike clinic's 15 among them, nor a hospital's own lines in its own stays; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-health.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:heart
contents[7]: "9 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "health_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, via) and the health_screen_links Dataset of four program-integrity screens", "4 saved views (referral concentration, billed in hospital or after death, strong-opioid prescribers, top-level visit billing)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on services billed during an admission or after death (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
